{"title":"Career Roadmap · Environmental Planner","role":"Environmental Planner","summary":"An Environmental Planner integrates environmental science, spatial planning, infrastructure planning and policy to ensure that development projects and urban/regional plans account for ecological, social and environmental impacts.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Plan (Bachelor of Planning)","Course":"Housing / Transport / Environmental Planning"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"An Environmental Planner integrates environmental science, spatial planning, infrastructure planning and policy to ensure that development projects and urban/regional plans account for ecological, social and environmental impacts."},{"type":"p","text":"For a B.Plan graduate, the strongest positioning is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Urban & Regional Planning","Environmental Planning","GIS","Ecology","Environmental Assessment","Climate Resilience"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"An Environmental Planner can work on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Environmental planning"},{"text":"Land-use planning"},{"text":"Environmental impact assessment support"},{"text":"Development planning"},{"text":"Environmental management plans"},{"text":"Climate-resilient planning"},{"text":"Natural-resource planning"},{"text":"Watershed planning"},{"text":"Green infrastructure"},{"text":"Biodiversity planning"},{"text":"Disaster-risk reduction"},{"text":"Sustainable transport and infrastructure"},{"text":"Environmental compliance"},{"text":"Urban sustainability"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The role is broader than environmental compliance alone. A strong planner should be able to translate environmental evidence into spatial plans, development strategies and practical mitigation measures."},{"type":"h","text":"Career Flow"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Plan","Urban + Regional Planning","Environmental Planning Fund